[38;2;255;248;220mSLAP #60 (P1, forge): Death animation uses self.age instead of self.death_timer. player.py:254 has frame_idx = int((self.age / 0.6) * 4) % 4 — but self.age is a monotonic counter incremented every tick by actor.tick_age() (line 170), so the death animation cycles at game-speed forever instead of playing once over 0.6s and holding the last frame. Meanwhile death_timer is initialized to 0.0, decremented in tick() (line 243), but never started (never set to 0.6 on death). The death frames spin rapidly and never settle. Rule: animation frame selection must use the dedicated timer, not a global monotonic counter. Fix: replace self.age with self.death_timer and set self.death_timer = 0.6 when alive flips to False, then hold the last frame when timer reaches 0.[0m
[38;2;255;248;220m[0m
[38;2;255;248;220mSLAP #61 (P2, forge): PROGRESS.md and BUILD-2026-09-13.md claim date 2026-09-13 but the system date is 2026-09-15 and all file timestamps are Sep 13 19:45-20:26. Docs date claims don't match reality, repeating STANDARDS P2 pattern from slaps #58/#59. The entry says "## 2026-09-13 — P4.2 Animation Depth (Forge)" while the session ran 2026-09-15.[0m
