[38;2;255;248;220mThe death animation bug (SLAP #60) is the biggest risk. When the player dies, the 4 death frames cycle rapidly at game tick rate forever — the player never visually dies, the animation never holds the final frame, and the death_timer that was meant to gate this is dead code. This is the core feature of P4.2 (4-frame death animation) and it's broken in the shipped state. Heads-up: the forge's session is still active and may fix this in its next turn; the acceptance command is python -m game.main --headless --turns 300 --seed 0 --verify (though the fix itself needs player.py code change: swap self.age → self.death_timer and set timer on death).[0m
